WEBVTT

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:03.255
A passage has a crucial phrase that one

00:00:03.275 --> 00:00:04.852
pooled vector may blur.

00:00:05.001 --> 00:00:07.559
Must we jointly encode it with every new

00:00:07.579 --> 00:00:09.826
query to preserve more detail?

00:00:10.014 --> 00:00:11.914
Predict what happens if we keep a set of

00:00:11.934 --> 00:00:13.538
token vectors instead.

00:00:15.953 --> 00:00:18.392
ColBERT style late interaction takes that

00:00:18.412 --> 00:00:21.098
route. Query and document are encoded

00:00:21.118 --> 00:00:23.508
independently, but comparison happens

00:00:23.528 --> 00:00:25.209
between their token vectors.

00:00:25.371 --> 00:00:27.722
We can prepare document representations in

00:00:27.742 --> 00:00:30.055
advance while preserving more local

00:00:30.075 --> 00:00:31.407
matching evidence.

00:00:32.317 --> 00:00:34.820
A conventional bi encoder produces one

00:00:34.840 --> 00:00:37.087
pooled vector per indexed unit.

00:00:37.211 --> 00:00:40.258
ColBERT retains vectors for tokens, then

00:00:40.278 --> 00:00:42.268
compares the query’s token vectors with

00:00:42.288 --> 00:00:44.292
the document’s token vectors after

00:00:44.312 --> 00:00:46.457
encoding. The tokens are contextual

00:00:46.477 --> 00:00:49.587
representations, not simple word counts.

00:00:50.141 --> 00:00:52.777
Late interaction can retrieve candidates

00:00:52.797 --> 00:00:55.921
or rerank an existing shortlist, depending

00:00:55.941 --> 00:00:58.073
on the implementation and scale.

00:00:58.248 --> 00:01:00.290
It generally needs more storage and

00:01:00.310 --> 00:01:02.957
computation than single vector retrieval,

00:01:03.080 --> 00:01:05.096
with less query time work than a full

00:01:05.116 --> 00:01:07.738
cross encoder over the same candidates.

00:01:08.626 --> 00:01:11.244
The chapter invents a tiny similarity

00:01:11.264 --> 00:01:14.195
table. Query tokens are citation and

00:01:14.215 --> 00:01:18.202
benefit. Document tokens are open, access,

00:01:18.326 --> 00:01:20.328
citation and advantage.

00:01:20.504 --> 00:01:23.757
Citation’s row is zero point one, zero

00:01:23.777 --> 00:01:26.708
point two, zero point nine, zero point

00:01:26.728 --> 00:01:27.390
four.

00:01:27.931 --> 00:01:30.952
Benefit’s row is zero point two, zero

00:01:30.972 --> 00:01:34.225
point three, zero point five, zero point

00:01:34.245 --> 00:01:37.575
eight. Keep the maximum in each query row:

00:01:37.725 --> 00:01:40.410
zero point nine and zero point eight.

00:01:40.572 --> 00:01:42.794
Add them to get one point seven.

00:01:42.969 --> 00:01:45.166
Those invented similarities illustrate

00:01:45.186 --> 00:01:47.923
MaxSim, not model measurements.

00:01:48.832 --> 00:01:51.579
The strongest alignment for citation is

00:01:51.599 --> 00:01:53.795
the document token citation.

00:01:53.958 --> 00:01:56.476
Benefit aligns most strongly with

00:01:56.496 --> 00:01:58.383
advantage in this table.

00:01:58.571 --> 00:02:00.587
The same document token could supply

00:02:00.607 --> 00:02:04.427
maxima for several query tokens; MaxSim

00:02:04.447 --> 00:02:06.836
does not enforce one to one matching.

00:02:07.405 --> 00:02:10.513
This decomposition shows which comparisons

00:02:10.533 --> 00:02:12.149
contributed to the score.

00:02:12.312 --> 00:02:13.890
It does not explain why the learnt

00:02:13.910 --> 00:02:16.622
contextual vectors considered those tokens

00:02:16.642 --> 00:02:19.482
similar. Inspectable scoring is not

00:02:19.502 --> 00:02:21.711
complete model transparency.

00:02:22.620 --> 00:02:25.039
Keeping one vector per token instead of

00:02:25.059 --> 00:02:28.815
one per passage multiplies storage roughly

00:02:28.835 --> 00:02:31.199
by the number of retained tokens, before

00:02:31.219 --> 00:02:33.763
compression. A toy hundred token passage

00:02:33.783 --> 00:02:36.302
would require a hundred vectors under that

00:02:36.322 --> 00:02:37.745
simplified accounting.

00:02:38.299 --> 00:02:40.686
The chapter reports ColBERT version two

00:02:40.706 --> 00:02:42.387
cutting earlier late interaction

00:02:42.407 --> 00:02:45.325
footprints six to tenfold with residual

00:02:45.345 --> 00:02:48.186
compression. This attributed comparison is

00:02:48.206 --> 00:02:50.698
not a promise for every index.

00:02:51.655 --> 00:02:53.877
Three arrangements are now visible.

00:02:54.039 --> 00:02:56.661
Independent pooled encoding compares one

00:02:56.681 --> 00:02:59.071
query vector with one stored passage

00:02:59.091 --> 00:03:02.589
vector. Joint encoding processes query and

00:03:02.609 --> 00:03:04.096
candidate together.

00:03:04.271 --> 00:03:07.138
Late interaction independently encodes

00:03:07.158 --> 00:03:09.457
sets of token vectors and compares them

00:03:09.477 --> 00:03:10.410
afterwards.

00:03:10.960 --> 00:03:13.243
A pretrained encoder can be adapted for

00:03:13.263 --> 00:03:14.634
different arrangements.

00:03:14.809 --> 00:03:17.083
Its name alone does not identify the

00:03:17.103 --> 00:03:18.320
retrieval system.

00:03:18.495 --> 00:03:21.542
Ask when query and document interact, what

00:03:21.562 --> 00:03:23.836
can be precomputed, what evidence the

00:03:23.856 --> 00:03:26.709
comparison retains, and which ranking task

00:03:26.729 --> 00:03:27.727
shaped training.

00:03:28.632 --> 00:03:31.392
Neural information retrieval also includes

00:03:31.412 --> 00:03:32.951
learnt sparse models.

00:03:33.126 --> 00:03:35.013
Their active vocabulary dimensions can

00:03:35.033 --> 00:03:37.410
contain both typed terms and learnt

00:03:37.430 --> 00:03:40.168
expansions, so an inverted index can serve

00:03:40.188 --> 00:03:43.776
them. A nonzero term matching score still

00:03:43.796 --> 00:03:46.404
requires overlap in active dimensions;

00:03:46.554 --> 00:03:48.234
expansion can create it.

00:03:48.795 --> 00:03:51.313
The chapter cites Elicit’s June twenty

00:03:51.333 --> 00:03:54.123
twenty four development work using SPLADE

00:03:54.143 --> 00:03:57.164
suggested terms with regular full text

00:03:57.184 --> 00:03:59.883
retrieval. That account does not confirm

00:03:59.903 --> 00:04:01.171
production deployment.

00:04:01.333 --> 00:04:03.659
Extra query terms can increase posting

00:04:03.679 --> 00:04:06.326
work and latency, even when the index

00:04:06.346 --> 00:04:08.452
technology is familiar.

00:04:09.341 --> 00:04:11.436
SPLADE can expose weighted vocabulary

00:04:11.456 --> 00:04:14.013
terms. ColBERT can expose token

00:04:14.033 --> 00:04:16.681
alignments. Both offer more scoring

00:04:16.701 --> 00:04:19.142
evidence than a single pooled score, while

00:04:19.162 --> 00:04:20.933
remaining dependent on training,

00:04:20.953 --> 00:04:23.665
vocabulary and transfer to the task.

00:04:23.814 --> 00:04:26.448
Neither is transparent from end to end.

00:04:27.015 --> 00:04:29.244
Neural is an umbrella label covering

00:04:29.264 --> 00:04:31.667
several representations and pipeline

00:04:31.687 --> 00:04:34.025
positions. Limited public deployment

00:04:34.045 --> 00:04:36.834
documentation for late interaction does

00:04:36.854 --> 00:04:38.973
not establish its absence.

00:04:39.135 --> 00:04:41.525
Identify the actual arrangement and

00:04:41.545 --> 00:04:44.643
evaluate the complete retrieval pipeline.
